cartridge "CHAMP DE CAROTTES/JEAN-FRANCOIS SEHAN/1984"

' CHAMP DE CAROTTES (the carrot field) - ColecoVision version of the Oric
' game by Jean-Francois Sehan ("L'Oric a l'affiche", Editions du P.S.I.,
' 1984). Adapted by Amy & Claude, Amy Studio 2026. Built by build.py from
' this file, ../_common/amy/core.alexis, pages.txt, art.py and music/*.txt.
'
' THE GAME (as in the book): a bitter winter day; Master Rabbit sees one
' last carrot at the far end of a snowy field. The villagers hid traps under
' the snow (invisible) and ringed the field with traps (visible). His
' detector shows how many traps lie on the four cells next to him (left,
' right, up, down; the border counts too). He hops one cell at a time and
' leaves a black square behind. A trap = lost (SHOOT), the carrot = won
' (ZAP); either way every trap is then shown. The book counts the moves.
'
' CONTROLS: joystick = hop one cell (up, down, left, right). Title: up/down
' choose, left/right change the starting level, a button confirms.
'
' LIBERTIES (listed for Amy):
' - Every visited cell keeps the detector's reading as a coloured disc with
'   dice pips (0 green, 1 ochre, 2 red, 3 magenta, 4 dark blue) instead of
'   the book's black square: the player reasons on the map, not on memory.
' - Three rabbits (lives, at most 5; one more every three fields). A hidden
'   trap snaps (shown in red), the rabbit squeals and hops back. A trap that
'   can be seen (sprung, or the border) is refused with a thump - the book
'   lost the game on a key slip into the border.
' - The rabbit stops when the detector beeps (1 or more): let go of the
'   stick and push again. Holding the stick on a clear cell keeps hopping.
' - Levels: the carrot is eaten, every trap is shown (the book's reveal),
'   then a new field with more traps (model/fieldsim.py and tests/bot.mjs
'   measured the table below). From field 2 the carrot and the start move.
' - A safe path always exists (a random walk is kept free while the traps
'   are hidden); the book's 100 random traps could wall the carrot off.
' - Field 26 x 19 inside the border (the Oric's 32 x 23): cols 3-28,
'   rows 3-21; the carrot on row 3, the rabbit starts on row 21, traps on
'   rows 4-20 (the book kept the carrot and start rows clear too).
' - Score: fewer hops = more points (the book's ESSAIS): bonus per field =
'   10 x level + (150 - hops) when under 150.
' - Colour, animation, music and sound effects are new.
' - v2: the seasons turn with the fields (a carrot field under snow all year
'   was odd): fields 1-2 spring (ploughed furrows, green and ochre, sprouts, blossoms, petals),
'   3-4 summer (grass, flowers, butterflies), 5-6 autumn (ochre ground,
'   russet leaves drifting), 7+ winter (snow, snowflakes). One colour table
'   per season and per screen third; one ambient particle kind per season
'   (2 sprites kept 96 lines apart: with the rabbit, 4 sprites a line at
'   most); a season card before every field. The traps grow faster
'   (30 at field 1, 144 from field 10; a rabbit back every 3 fields).

' tile set Cc: 45 tiles from code 128 (generated by art.py)

